fair-costermongers-sealed-7day-trace.jsonl
demo-stderr.log

# the record of a live run, which is none of those things: not deterministic,
# not regenerated, and not recoverable once gone. Ignored so it is never
# committed, and deliberately absent from `make clean`.
live-trace.jsonl
# the service's trace is the same kind of record — the conversations strangers
# had with a built agent, word for word — and on top of that not public.
service-trace.jsonl

# episode state
*.db
*.sqlite

# Python bytecode. A guest that splits itself into modules — or imports another
# guest, as examples/guests/rival.py does — makes CPython write one of these
# next to the source the first time it runs.
__pycache__/

# macOS Finder
.DS_Store
# SQLite writes these next to any open database; they are process state, not data.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local tooling state: the Browser-pane launch configs, and the scratch git
# worktrees agent sessions leave behind — each of which is a whole second copy
# of this repo, so an unguarded `git add -A` would otherwise sweep one in.
.claude/
